I have just finished my final presentation for the IBM TU in Cairns.

Each presentation was scheduled for 3 hours, 90 minutes of lecture and 90 
minutes of hands-on lab exercises with a 30 minute break in between.

I gave two presentations, one titled "Introduction to SE Linux" and the other 
"Writing SE Linux Policy".  The introduction lecture + lab was scheduled 
twice, while the policy writing one was only scheduled once due to less 
demand for the more advanced course.

The Introduction to SE Linux went mostly to schedule as the lecture was 
similar to what I have given before and the lab exercises had been tested by 
several people before the conference.

The Policy writing lecture went for about 2 hours and the lab came to an 
abrupt end after almost 2 hours when I had to vacate the room for the next 
lecture (the students only completed about 70% of the material in that time).

In the near future I will put all the lecture and lab notes on the web and 
announce it here.

